    "created_at": "2015-12-21T18:06:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-12-21T18:33:58Z",
    "body": "The problem is that `next`, `previous`, `before` and `after` aren't verbs.\n\nThis kind of names (adverbs, adjectives) historically return booleans. I read `sibling.after(otherSibling)` as `sibling.isAfter(otherSibling)`.\n\nWould it be too bad to have `pullsBefore`, `pullsAfter` instead? They are nearly as short and they make more sense.\n\nOther options:\n\n```\nsibling.getsBefore(aSibling)\nsibling.takesBefore(aSibling)\nsibling.pullsBefore(aSibling)\nsibling.obtainsBefore(aSibling)\nsibling.grabsBefore(aSibling)\nsibling.picksBefore(aSibling)\n```\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/dom/issues/comments/166376842/reactions",
